  <title>Attaching a scanned file</title>

  <p>Several windows keep a PDF with a record: a vendor's invoice, a signed
  tax exemption, a purchase order. They all attach it with the same
  window.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Either choose the scanner under <gui>Scan file to attach</gui>
    and click <gui>Scan</gui>, or choose a PDF under <gui>Attach file from
    disk</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>PyGtk Posting makes a smaller copy of the file, and shows the
    size of both beside <gui>Original file</gui> and <gui>Optimized
    file</gui>. The smaller one is chosen; click the other to see and use it
    instead.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check the file in the preview, and click
    <gui>Attach</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>If the smaller copy cannot be made, a message says so and the original
  file is used; it can still be attached.</p>

</page>
